   {
    "id": "story",
    "type": "story",
    "provenance": "original",
    "title": {
     "en": "Two answers"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Mina worked out 2 + 3 × 4. She added first and got 20. Her friend multiplied first and got 14.\n\"Who is right?\" they asked the teacher.\n\"The one who multiplied first,\" she said. \"There is an order to follow.\""
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "expression",
     "bracket",
     "order of operations",
     "evaluate"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "When an expression has more than one operation, we follow an order: first brackets, then multiplication and division from left to right, then addition and subtraction from left to right.\nSo 2 + 3 × 4 = 2 + 12 = 14. With brackets, (2 + 3) × 4 = 5 × 4 = 20. Brackets change the order.\nOperations of the same rank, such as multiplication and division, are done from left to right. For example 24 ÷ 4 × 2 = 6 × 2 = 12."
    }
   },
